# Target C: actual-state realization constraint for eight-no-root `k=6, D=-1` Profile B

Date: 2026-09-22

Status: rigorous strengthening of the fixed-nine-block Profile B audit. No closure is claimed until the full finite cover executes.

Companion verifier:

`research/verify_target_c_support7_global_segment_relative_eight_noroot_k6_dminus1_profile_b_actual_state_realization_2026_09_22.py`

It wraps the current fixed-nine verifier:

`research/verify_target_c_support7_global_segment_relative_eight_noroot_k6_dminus1_profile_b_fixed_nine_basis_2026_09_22.py`.

## 1. What the fixed-nine audit still does not enforce

The fixed-nine audit requires one set of nine compatible singleton blocks to form the replacement-functional basis at eight rows and to descend with the required ranks through the selected clean `8 -> 7 -> 6 -> 5` puncture fan.

There are two additional identity constraints. First, those same nine singleton states must generate the prescribed rank-two coefficient plane. Second, the global nine-set must extend one of the exact seven-block bases already selected at the synchronized six-row seed; it is not enough that an unrelated nine-set happens to work at the restored source.

A Profile B root state has

```text
p = 9,
q = 9,
nine singleton replacements of virtual-complete blocks.
```

Those nine singletons already use all nine incomplete root rows. Therefore every virtual-empty block stays empty, every unchosen virtual-complete block stays complete, and the coefficient-constraint space generated by those actual block states must be exactly the prescribed rank-two plane `P_8`.

Individual singleton compatibility gives only

```text
L_b <= P_8
```

for each chosen block. It does not by itself imply that the actual selected block states generate all of `P_8`.

## 2. Source realization criterion

Fix an eight-row virtual state with rank-two coefficient plane `P`. Let

- `G` be its compatible singleton virtual-complete blocks;
- `f_b` be the replacement-functional class of `b in G` in the nine-dimensional canonical functional quotient `V`;
- `L_b <= P` be the local coefficient-constraint space of that singleton state;
- `E <= P` be the span of the empty-state constraints of all virtual-empty blocks.

Singleton compatibility on a virtual-complete block is unique, so `f_b` and `L_b` are unambiguous.

The global rank-nine condition is

```text
span{f_b : b in G} = V,
dim V = 9.
```

A genuine Profile B source state requires a nine-block set `B subset G` satisfying both

```text
{f_b : b in B} is a basis of V,                 (2.1)
E + sum_{b in B} L_b = P.                       (2.2)
```

Equation (2.2) is the actual-state coefficient condition.

## 3. Rank-two seed lemma

Because `dim P = 2`, existence of a source realization has a small exact certificate.

> **Lemma.** Assume the compatible singleton classes span `V`. A nine-block set satisfying (2.1)-(2.2) exists if and only if there is a set `S subset G`, with `|S| <= 2`, such that
>
> ```text
> E + sum_{b in S} L_b = P,
> {f_b : b in S} is linearly independent in V.       (3.1)
> ```

If `B` satisfies (2.1)-(2.2), choose `S subset B` minimal with

```text
E + sum_{b in S} L_b = P.
```

Each `L_b` has dimension at most one and `P/E` has dimension at most two, so `|S| <= 2`. Since `S` is a subset of the functional basis `B`, its classes are independent.

Conversely, suppose `S` satisfies (3.1). The ground set `{f_b : b in G}` spans the rank-nine linear matroid `V`. Every independent set in a linear matroid extends to a basis using elements of the same ground set, so `S` extends to a nine-block functional basis `B`. Every `L_b` lies inside `P`; since the seed already generates `P` together with `E`, adding the remaining basis blocks preserves equality with `P`. Thus `B` satisfies (2.1)-(2.2).

This gives a cheap necessary-and-sufficient source prefilter: check only seeds of sizes zero, one, and two rather than first enumerating all nine-block subsets.

## 4. Fixed seven-block six-row basis must extend to the source

The synchronized six-row audit does not merely say that some seven singleton classes span. Its exact common-basis filter returns specific seven-block sets whose classes form a six-row basis and whose images span every required five-row puncture quotient.

Let `B_7` be one such seven-block set for the current six-row seed. If a genuine global Profile B realization restores this seed, the source classes on those same seven blocks must be compatible with the same singleton states and remain independent. Linear puncture maps cannot increase rank, while their six-row images have rank seven, so

```text
rank{f_b : b in B_7} = 7
```

at the eight-row source.

The global profile has exactly two additional singleton blocks, say `x,y`. Hence this particular six-row basis extends to a genuine source only if

```text
rank({f_b : b in B_7} union {f_x,f_y}) = 9
```

and

```text
E + sum_{b in B_7} L_b + L_x + L_y = P.
```

The strengthened verifier now carries every exact six-row common-basis identity into the two-row lift. Before the fixed-nine enumeration it requires at least one such seven-block basis to admit two extra source singleton blocks satisfying both conditions. During the fixed-nine rank test, the chosen global nine-set must actually contain one of those source-extendable seven-block bases.

This closes a consistency gap left by the earlier fixed-nine wrapper: an unrelated source nine-set can no longer certify a lift of a six-row state whose actual seven-class basis does not extend globally.

## 5. Same-nine-set coefficient enforcement

The rank-two seed lemma and fixed-seven extension test only prove source-level existence. The clean-fan constraints must hold for the same nine blocks.

Inside the fixed-nine source-rank test, the wrapper intercepts each particular chosen nine-block set and reconstructs the actual state:

```text
virtual-empty blocks     -> empty,
chosen nine blocks       -> their unique singleton states,
other virtual-complete   -> complete.
```

It computes the exact coefficient space generated by all those block states and requires

```text
P_actual = P_8.
```

Only after this equality holds is the chosen set allowed to enter the existing exact rank-nine and puncture-fan tests. Thus the coefficient-space realization, the fixed six-row basis identity, and the clean-fan functional basis are required of the same global nine-block set.

## 6. Independent defect check

For every chosen nine-set that realizes `P_8` and has source functional rank nine, the wrapper rebuilds the actual eight-row relation matrix using the actual block states, computes its rank over `Q`, and checks directly that

```text
number_of_rows - 3 * relation_rank = -1.
```

This is logically redundant with the maximal replacement-functional accounting if all preceding formulas are used correctly, but it is an independent implementation check on the reconstructed state.

## 7. Finite consequence

A genuine Profile B state must pass all of the following simultaneously:

1. the original global rank-two clean-lift conditions;
2. one exact seven-block common basis from the synchronized six-row seed;
3. extension of that same seven-block basis by exactly two source singleton blocks to functional rank nine and coefficient span `P_8`;
4. a fixed nine-block functional basis through all selected clean punctures;
5. the rank-two source seed criterion;
6. exact coefficient-space realization by that same chosen nine-block set; and
7. direct exact defect `-1` for the reconstructed actual state.

Therefore a full-cover zero-survivor result from the companion verifier excludes Profile B rigorously.

If a survivor remains, it now contains an explicit fixed nine-singleton root state that extends an exact six-row common basis, generates the prescribed coefficient plane, satisfies the selected puncture fan, and has exact local defect `-1`. Such a survivor needs a different structural obstruction rather than another source-identity consistency test.

No census result is claimed here. The available GitHub Actions runs are still failing before runner acquisition, so this note records the sharpened finite target rather than a closure result.
